WEBVTT

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.030
We've finally made it to this point.

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:16.030
<i>After countless trials, the time has come...</i>

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.910
<b>Inaugural

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:23.530
<i>The diabolical game created at 
President Hyoudou's request!</i>

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:27.040
<b>Inaugural
Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors Game
Final Outline</b>

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:26.300
<i>The first ever game of Restricted 
Rock Paper Scissors!</i>

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:27.040
<b>Authorized by the President</b>

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.790
<b>Meeting Room 3</b>

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.430
Gentlemen, you've done 
well to bring us this far.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.820
As your team leader, I want to thank you.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:35.680
Sir!

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.180
And to reward you, today we're having 
a bowling party to wrap things up.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.390
Or rather, I'd like to do that,

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:47.190
but it'll have to wait until 
after the game tomorrow.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.820
I can't have you all showing 
up late again, after all.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:55.820
Aw, sir, don't bring that up again.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.570
Tonegawa-san!

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:02.050
Let's make the first game of 
Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors a success!

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:02.950
Tonegawa-sensei!

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:03.610
Sensei!

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:04.170
Sensei!

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:04.750
Sensei!

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:05.240
Sensei!

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:07.210
Sensei!

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.460
Sensei!

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:14.000
<i>Their unity and anticipation are on the rise!</i>

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:18.720
<b>Unity!</b>

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:18.720
<b>Anticipation!!</b>

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.720
<i>The stage is set for Team Tonegawa, 
and they're ready for tomorrow's big game!</i>

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:18.720
<b>The stage is set!</b>

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:23.970
Hello?

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.390
<i>Tonegawa, it's me.</i>

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.480
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.480
President Hyoudou?!

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:35.990
<i>Tonegawa Yukio, the number two 
man of the massive Teiai Group.</i>

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:40.490
<b>President's Office</b>

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:40.140
<i>This is the story of the battles</i>

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:45.050
<i>he waged as a middle manager, in the 
shadows of the glory and fame he achieved...</i>

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:51.720
<i>The small, unremarkable story... 
about the struggles of a remarkable man.</i>

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:52.500
Okay.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:02.810
<i>Agenda 13:
</i>Setting Sail

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.770
You called, President Hyoudou?

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:08.770
The preparations for 
Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors are—

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.770
Tonegawa. Tell me.

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:13.400
Do you respect me?

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.480
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:17.210
That goes without saying, sir.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:20.450
You are a grand figure, 
and respected as such.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:24.920
Well, I suppose you can say 
whatever you want. Talk is cheap.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:26.910
N-No, sir, I would never—

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:26.910
Silence!

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.420
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:36.050
No matter what you say, there could 
be hate deep down in your guts.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.680
You might be laughing at me 
with your tongue stuck out.

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:44.200
I've seen so many people 
like that, it makes me sick.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.430
N-No, sir, I promise it's not like that!

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:51.310
<b>Loyalty</b>

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.310
Then what do you say I test your loyalty?

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:59.570
<b>Loyalty</b>

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:59.570
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:59.570
<i>T-Test my loyalty? 
What exactly is he going to do?</i>

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.510
One day, you find yourself 
walking through the woods,

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:07.610
the ground thick with grass,
as insects sing all around you.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.260
And then, suddenly,

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:15.860
from the brush, an animal 
jumps into your path.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:20.010
Now, what animal is it?

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:22.610
<i>I-I have no idea what this 
is supposed to prove...</i>

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:24.840
<i>But if I upset the president now,</i>

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.250
<i>he may cancel tomorrow's 
Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors game</i>

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:30.020
<i>or come up with some crazy new demand!</i>

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:31.640
<i>I must answer...</i>

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:34.450
<i>An animal that won't upset the president...</i>

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:37.400
<i>In terms of creatures you'd 
run into in the woods...</i>

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.730
<i>A bear!</i>

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:41.610
<i>No! That's too pedestrian!</i>

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:44.220
<i>I'll tailor it to suit his tastes...</i>

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.640
<i>A tiger?!</i>

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:48.530
<i>No! It'd be obvious I'm appealing to him...</i>

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:53.040
<i>D-Damn it, I don't know! 
I don't know how to answer!</i>

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:57.000
Don't overthink it. Give the first 
answer that comes to your mind.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.920
Th-Then...

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.390
A rabbit!

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:03.630
<i>Tonegawa goes with the flow,</i>

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:08.180
<b>Instinct!</b>

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:08.180
<i>believing in his instincts and 
entrusting his fate to a bunny!</i>

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:08.180
<b>Fate!</b>

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:13.520
I see...

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.580
Tonegawa,

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:18.610
despite your appearance, it seems...

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:22.650
you're quite the romantic. The type who's 
in love with the idea of being in love.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:24.040
<b>The Romantic Type</b>

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.040
I-In love?!

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:26.370
Question two!

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.550
Tomorrow is the play you've 
been rehearsing for.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:32.880
A-Actually, sir, tomorrow is the day of the—

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.500
Do not interrupt me!

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:38.880
You're going to make me lose my place.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.420
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:41.480
It can't be...

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:46.340
<i>He's into psychological tests now?!</i>

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:47.800
<b>Psychological Tests</b>

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:47.800
~Now you can figure him out~

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:47.800
<i>At his age?!</i>

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.410
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:53.830
Then, during the performance,

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:58.230
you, playing the king, glance at 
the actress playing the princess...

00:04:58.230 --> 00:04:59.190
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:01.230
<b>Shock</b>

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:01.230
and are shocked.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:05.640
Tell me... why are you shocked?

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:08.070
Answer! Now!

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:14.770
B-Because she's a woman of more... 
advanced age than I anticipated?

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:16.490
What color are her shoes?

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:19.130
What is the color of the shoes 
the actress is wearing?

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.190
Wh-White?

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:28.590
That badly, eh?

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:32.070
An older woman with white shoes, eh?

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:37.220
So that's how you see me...

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:39.120
You're rather attached, aren't you?

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:41.740
Here! Look at this!

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:42.480
Sir.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:45.990
Oh, my...

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:49.190
Right? Right? You see what I'm talking about?

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:53.690
<i>Wh-Wh-What?! What does it say?!</i>

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.000
Now, question three.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:56.870
<i>It's still going?!</i>

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:59.670
You are an astronaut,

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:03.730
but because of a malfunction, 
you must make an emergency landing.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:07.130
<b>Certain</b>

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:08.650
You exit your ship on a 
certain planet to find...

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:12.510
An alien! An inhabitant of that world.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:16.770
Tell me... what does that alien look like?

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:19.270
Answer within three seconds.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:21.950
Three... two... one...

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:23.730
An... An octopus!

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:27.650
It's a giant octopus-like 
alien, with many legs!

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.700
<b>Hold on...</b>

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:38.660
Tonegawa... what color is 
this octoid alien of yours?

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:46.320
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.570
Color...?

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:45.320
Color... color... color?

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:49.470
Red? A reddish color...

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:54.040
Red, red, red, red...

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:58.680
You bastard!

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:02.690
That's what you've been thinking?!

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.710
You insolent fool! Take your punishment!

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:07.100
Punishment! Punishment!

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:09.250
I didn't mean red!

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:12.870
Blue! I meant to say blue, sir!

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:20.210
<b>Shudder... Shudder... Shudder...</b>

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:19.160
B-Blue?!

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:24.020
What kind of blue?

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:26.720
Uh, I'm not sure...

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:30.220
Let's see... a purplish... maybe...

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:35.520
All of you, look here! Bluish purple...

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:36.050
Sir.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.440
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:47.940
<b>Shudder... Shudder... Shudder...</b>

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:47.940
Wh-What's the matter, sir?

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:51.200
What does bluish purple mean?

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:54.450
<b>Shudder... Shudder... Shudder...</b>

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:55.030
Stop!

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:59.990
I've seen all manner of 
degenerates in my time,

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:02.830
but you, Tonegawa...

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:06.260
You're the winner, 
the biggest degenerate of them all!

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:08.090
<b>Degenerate?</b>

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:08.090
<b>Winner?</b>

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:08.090
De—

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:11.020
Come on, all of you, congratulate the man.

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:11.510
Sir!

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:13.720
<b>Celebrating</b>

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:18.350
Congratulations! Congratulations! 
Congratulations!

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:23.070
<i>Congratulations! Tonegawa is the winner!</i>

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:26.490
<i>And Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors 
is confirmed for tomorrow!</i>

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:28.610
<i>He's relieved from his anxieties! And yet...</i>

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:33.610
<i>Wh-What exactly did it say 
about bluish purple?</i>

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:37.860
<i>He's vexed. Overwhelmingly vexed.</i>

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:43.620
<i>The next day... Tonight, it finally begins!</i>

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:46.310
<i>The fruit of Team Tonegawa's efforts!</i>

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:51.030
<i>The first game of Restricted 
Rock-Paper-Scissors!</i>

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:58.400
It's finally time, Tonegawa.

00:08:58.400 --> 00:08:59.260
Yes, sir.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:03.520
I'm sure you'll find it to 
be an enjoyable night.

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:10.810
<i>On the boat of hope, </i>Espoir<i>,</i>

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:19.350
<i>the voyage that will decide the fate 
of Tonegawa and the debtors now begins!</i>

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:34.750
<i>A single night of gambling for 
people at their wit's end.</i>

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:37.890
<i>Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors!</i>

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:44.980
You'll be playing 
Rock-Paper-Scissors with 12 cards,

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:49.400
wagering the stars on your chest, like so.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:54.940
Once cards are used, 
they're deposited in the box.

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:59.320
They are then automatically counted,

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:04.080
with the total displayed on 
the electronic scoreboard.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.260
The duration will be four hours.

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:10.750
Regardless of how you get there, 
if you have three stars at the end

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.090
and are able to use up all 
your cards, you win.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:15.860
This game is that simple.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:19.340
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:24.780
<i>Master of ceremonies Tonegawa 
completes his explanation of the rules,</i>

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:26.350
<i>and the game begins!</i>

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:32.680
I wish you all the best of luck.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:35.730
<b>However!</b>

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:35.730
<i>However!</i>

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:37.160
This is crap!

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:40.060
You haven't told us how we're 
supposed to use the money you lent us!

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:41.870
And what happens if we lose?!

00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:45.620
That's right! Explain, damn it!

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:46.800
What happens, old man?!

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:50.120
<i>Jeers are flying! The debtors are revolting!</i>

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:54.380
Fuck you!

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:57.130
I'll kill you, you bunch of trash!

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:09.270
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:13.800
<i>He saw this coming. A bit of 
booing won't shake Tonegawa.</i>

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:18.100
<i>If anything, he launches a lecture that 
makes it seem like he was waiting for this!</i>

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:20.030
You need to throw away your weakness!

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:24.580
All of you are here because 
you're losers in society.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:29.790
You could say that you've all 
fallen off the stairway to Heaven!

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:34.170
What you should be doing now is winning!

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:36.670
If you don't win, you're trash!

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:44.680
Nomo is a half-wit. Habu is a downer.

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.680
<b>*This is his personal opinion.</b>

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:45.180
<b>*He means it in a good way.</b>

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:48.680
Ichiro is a self-absorbed son of a bitch.

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:48.680
<b>*According to rumors.</b>

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:49.810
And yet!

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:55.800
No one says that about them, not only 
because of their incredible talent,

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:58.070
but because they're winners!

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:01.570
What's the point in worrying 
about what happens if you lose?!

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:04.070
You have to win!

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:07.200
You need to win! You must win!

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:13.210
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:15.690
He's right!

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:19.210
I'm gonna win! I'm gonna win this thing!

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:28.100
<i>It shifts! Tonegawa's speech causes a shift 
in the anxious energy filling the crowd!</i>

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.100
<i>And as a result...</i>

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:36.730
You bastard! Give me that star back!

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:37.910
Calm down!

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:46.610
Hey! I heard something in there!

00:12:46.610 --> 00:12:48.390
Are they cheating?!

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:55.850
<i>They fight to survive! 
In order to reign as the winner,</i>

00:12:55.850 --> 00:13:01.510
<i>they reveal their true natures as they 
enter an ugly, desperate, bitter struggle!</i>

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:04.010
<i>A vision of Hell! It's a vision of Hell!</i>

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:02.900
<b>A vision of hell!!</b>

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:04.010
<b>A vision of hell!!</b>

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:07.510
<b>A vision of hell!!</b>

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:06.840
<i>It could be called nothing else!</i>

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:13.540
This is fantastic. Truly fantastic!

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:16.360
I'm thrilled, Tonegawa.

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:17.020
Sir.

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.010
All right, it's settled.

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:23.210
The second game will be 
held three days from now!

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:25.860
Goodnight.

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:27.910
But...

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:31.850
<i>In spite of that, the first game 
of Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors</i>

00:13:31.850 --> 00:13:34.160
<i>comes to a successful conclusion!</i>

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:41.410
That was amazing, sir.

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:44.150
What're you talking about?

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:46.490
I mean your speech, of course!

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.520
Did you just ad-lib all of that?

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:51.930
Come on, that was nothing.

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:54.180
Besides...

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:59.200
I told those debtors that they had 
fallen from the stairway to Heaven,

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.190
but that wasn't intense enough.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:05.940
There was never any such 
stairway for filth like them.

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:09.200
This is a cauldron in the pits of Hell.

00:14:10.310 --> 00:14:12.490
To push them in makes for better motivation.

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:14.330
I see!

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:17.860
Even so, sir, I doubt most people 
could come across as so amazing.

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:21.370
Especially when you shut 
all of them up by saying...

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:23.310
"Fakku yoo!"

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:25.880
"I'm gonna murder you, you specks of dust!"

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:28.400
That was terrifying!

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:32.690
Wrong. It's not "Fakku yoo." 
It's "Fuck you!"

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:31.360
<b>Fakku yoo</b>

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:36.410
And it was "I'll kill you, 
you bunch of trash!"

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.410
<b>I'm gonna murder you, you specks of dust!"</b>

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.410
<b>I'll kill you, you bunch of trash!!</b>

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:40.650
You choice of words is always so 
rugged! Your pronunciation, too!

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:43.150
Oh, stop it.

00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:44.410
Well, let's head back.

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:48.550
We've chit-chatted long enough.
The wind is chilly tonight.

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:49.400
Wait, sir!

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:54.250
What is the key to giving 
a speech, in your opinion?

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:01.540
You fool...

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:07.130
You get me talking about that, 
and we'll be here all night.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:08.670
I'd love to hear it!

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:13.430
<i>A sense of fulfillment! As they are 
gently caressed by the sea breeze,</i>

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:17.080
<i>they continue to chat... until the morning.</i>

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:22.180
<b>Three Days Later</b>

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.180
<i>Three days later...</i>

00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:26.570
<i>It's already time for the second game 
of Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors!</i>

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:29.820
<i>With 90 contestants, 
including return players!</i>

00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:33.320
<i>They've managed to put together 
another group of debtors!</i>

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:34.910
<i>And...</i>

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:37.830
Can't squeeze out any more...

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:41.520
<i>President Hyoudou shocks the room 
by falling into a deep sleep!</i>

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:45.840
<i>He departs on his own ship, 
to the world of dreams.</i>

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:48.660
<i>This relieves them of all pressure!</i>

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:51.340
<i>The second game is sure 
to go off without a hitch!</i>

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:52.590
<b>And yet!</b>

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:52.590
<i>And yet!</i>

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:55.100
N-No way!

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:57.120
The salty air
messed up
my throat

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:01.830
You lost your voice, Tonegawa-sensei?!

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:06.900
Yamazaki, you're the only one
who can do this.
The others are
all inside the boxes.

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:12.780
Th-That's true... Everyone else is 
inside the tables, counting the cards.

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:16.330
O-Oh, no!

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:17.910
<b>An unexpected accident!</b>

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:19.000
<i>An unexpected accident...</i>

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:22.370
<i>gives rise to the new master 
of ceremonies: Yamazaki!</i>

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:24.080
<b>MC Yamazaki</b>

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:23.330
<i>However!</i>

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:28.850
<i>Will he make it in time if he starts 
practicing now?! There's 35 minutes to go!</i>

00:16:28.850 --> 00:16:32.870
Fuh... Fakku Yoo? Fack Yew?

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:34.090
Not "Fack yew,"
"Fuck you"

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:34.090
F... Fuck?

00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:35.990
<i>Five minutes to go!</i>

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:38.420
Uh... If you can't win...

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:42.730
Ichiro is a self-absorbed bastard... 
and Habu is a half-wit...

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:45.350
Self absorbed son of a bitch -> Ichiro
Downer->Habu
Half Wit->Nomo

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:45.350
Oh, Nomo's the half-wit.

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:47.360
<i>And now... it's showtime.</i>

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:53.360
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:56.610
So, I'm the master of—

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:58.690
H-Huh?

00:16:58.690 --> 00:17:00.740
Check, check. Mic check!

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:03.620
<i>Despite this unfortunate accident...</i>

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:08.630
Relax

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:13.050
I will now explain the rules.

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:17.680
<i>Yamazaki manages to successfully 
explain the rules.</i>

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:23.930
I wish you all the best of health... 
I mean, the best of luck.

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:26.900
<i>It seems he's managed to 
wrap it up successfully.</i>

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:27.940
<i>However!</i>

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:30.380
Wait, what's the money for?

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:32.570
And what happens to us if we lose?

00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:34.520
Yeah, what happens then?! 
You better explain!

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:41.080
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:36.580
Don't mess with us! Come on!

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:37.360
<i>Here we go.</i>

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.570
You want me to come up there?!

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:39.910
<i>This is it.</i>

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:51.710
Fuck you! I'll kill you, you bunch of trash!

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:56.720
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:00.390
<i>All right! He pulled it off!</i>

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:03.210
<i>That's the first hurdle down.</i>

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:09.650
A-All of you are here because 
you're losers in society.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:13.230
What you should be doing now is winning!

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:15.610
<b>If you don't win, you're trash!</b>

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:15.610
If you don't win, you're trash!

00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:17.480
<i>Psst... Psst...</i>

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:19.870
Yeah... Gotta win... There's no other way...

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:20.990
I wanna win!

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:22.550
I should win!

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:23.190
I'm gonna win!

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:25.870
<b>Course Correction!</b>

00:18:23.190 --> 00:18:25.870
<i>The course is corrected! Their 
swelling resentment has vanished!</i>

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:31.130
<i>Though Yamazaki might not be used 
to handling the helm of the ship,</i>

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:35.630
<i>he manages to steer the debtors 
away from their resistance!</i>

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:40.930
N-Nomo is a down—

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:48.440
...half-wit. And Ichiro... Ichiro is...

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:50.400
a self-absorbed son of a bitch!

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:53.030
<i>Good, very good! Keep it up!</i>

00:18:53.030 --> 00:18:53.740
Habu is...

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:54.900
Hey, asshole!

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:59.800
You piece of crap! Don't mock Ichiro!

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:03.960
What the hell do you know about him?!

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:05.660
A-An Ichiro fan?!

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:08.910
Yeah! That's right! Ichiro rules!

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:12.670
<i>There's sudden turbulence 
as the debtors lash out!</i>

00:19:09.180 --> 00:19:12.670
<b>Turbulence!</b>

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:12.670
<b>The Debtors Lash Out!</b>

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:14.670
Just talk about
Habu instead!

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:16.560
You oughta apologize to Nomo, too!

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:18.050
Don't you mess with Ichiro!

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:21.610
I get it! Ichiro is great!

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:24.930
And Nomo is a real pioneer! But Habu...

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:28.410
<i>There was one hidden amongst the masses!</i>

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:30.810
King

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:30.260
<i>A supremely devoted shogi fan!</i>

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:32.810
Say something, damn it!

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:35.000
What's the matter, half-wit?!

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:38.820
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:37.290
Y-You have to win...

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:38.820
What's the matter, sunglasses?!

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:41.120
You want us to tear you apart?!

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:42.820
What are you, a crash test dummy?!

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:46.600
Y-You have to... have to...

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:48.700
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:48.700
W-Wi... w...

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:50.580
Who wants to win?!

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:55.710
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:19:57.650 --> 00:19:59.960
Fool! Don't do it, Yamazaki!

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:03.220
If you win, you rise to Heaven! 
Lose, and you fall to Hell!

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:05.470
Y-You're making this sound like...

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:06.740
It sounds like...

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:10.230
Who wants to be like Ichiro?!

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:11.980
It sounds like...

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:15.380
That old show, <i>Ultra Quiz</i>!

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:22.990
<i>Thanks to Yamazaki's speech, 
the game is a huge success,</i>

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:25.210
<i>albeit one with a totally 
different atmosphere!</i>

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:25.210
Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:27.030
<i>The second game goes off without a hitch!</i>

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:39.500
Congratulations!

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:44.010
Reserved for
Teiai Finance

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:44.010
<i>And so it begins: a raucously 
celebratory wrap-up party!</i>

00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:47.690
<i>Tonegawa has struggled between 
his employer, the president,</i>

00:20:47.690 --> 00:20:50.030
<i>and his own employees, the men in black,</i>

00:20:50.030 --> 00:20:53.270
<i>to make this once-in-a-lifetime 
project a success.</i>

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:58.270
<b>Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors Complete!
Congratulations!</b>

00:20:55.010 --> 00:20:58.270
<i>The diabolical death game, 
Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors...</i>

00:20:58.970 --> 00:21:02.030
<i>has now been... completed!</i>

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:12.040
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:12.040
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:22:34.600 --> 00:22:37.040
<i>And some time later...</i>

00:22:37.400 --> 00:22:40.950
<i>This man, Kaiji, will give rise</i>

00:22:41.570 --> 00:22:44.030
<i>to a legend that will overwhelm them all.</i>

00:22:55.110 --> 00:22:57.350
<i>Next time, "Excursion."</i>

00:22:56.160 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Excursion</b>
